  hintId: tutorial_syntax
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Syntax
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'Syntax is the set of rules used to write instructions for processing
    data and controlling robotic systems.

    Every command must follow the correct
    structure in order to be understood and executed properly by the robot.


    Using
    syntax correctly allows you to:

    <indent=2em>- Process information from the
    environment</indent>

    <indent=2em>- Make decisions using logic and conditions</indent>

    <indent=2em>-
    Automate complex behaviors</indent>


    Syntax examples include variables,
    conditionals, loops, and lists, along with many other programming structures.


    Even
    small syntax mistakes may cause commands to fail or produce unexpected results.

    Understanding
    syntax is an important step in learning programming, as it teaches how instructions
    are structured and interpreted by a system.'
  isImageBig: 0
